\section{Creating self-contained functions}{


Self-contained likelihood and prior functions should follow these
guidelines:
\enumerate{
\item Call package functions with explicit \code{::} namespaces, e.g.
\code{extraDistr::qtnorm()}. Alternatively, call \code{library()} inside the function
if you need to attach a package.
\item Declare all data dependencies explicitly, similar to the pattern used in
\link{create_likelihood}.
\item Any helper functions (closures) called within a self-contained function
must itself be self-contained.
